Red Dog is a 2011 Australian comedy-drama family film written by Daniel Taplitz,
directed by Kriv Stenders and produced by Nelson Woss and Julie Ryan.

11
00:53:15,789 --> 00:53:21,789
It stars Koko as the title character, Josh Lucas,
Rachael Taylor, and John Batchelor.

12
00:58:06,315 --> 00:58:12,315
The film is based on the true story of Red Dog and uses the 2002 novel
Red Dog by Louis de Bernières as the primary source.

13
01:02:56,842 --> 01:03:02,842
At the 2011 Inside Film Awards, Red Dog was nominated in nine
categories and won seven, including best feature film.

14
01:07:47,368 --> 01:07:53,368
The film was also nominated for seven AACTA Awards and won for Best Film.

15
01:12:37,894 --> 01:12:43,894
The film was theatrically released on 4 August
2011 by Roadshow Film Distributors.

16
01:17:28,421 --> 01:17:34,421
The film was followed by a prequel, Red Dog: True Blue released in 2016, and a
spin-off documentary Koko: A Red Dog Story released in 2019.

17
01:22:18,947 --> 01:22:24,947
The film explores themes of australia, 1970s, human animal
relationship, search, based on true story.

18
01:27:09,473 --> 01:27:15,473
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
